          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>A long week of reading. I am still working my way through <fr:link href="/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" title="Gödel, Escher, Bach: An Eternal Goden Braid" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" display-uri="hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999" type="local">GEB</fr:link>, but it has become significantly more dense as we get to more formal mathematics. I will be starting <fr:link href="/macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018/" title="The Spy and the Traitor: An incredible espionage and spy thriller and the greatest true story of the Cold War" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018/" display-uri="macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018" type="local">The Spy and the Traitor: An incredible espionage and spy thriller and the greatest true story of the Cold War</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link>
                  </fr:author>
                </fr:authors>
                <fr:date>
                  <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
                  <fr:month>7</fr:month>
                  <fr:day>28</fr:day>
                </fr:date>
                <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/4SOC/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>4SOC</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/4SOC/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Review: Candide">Review: <fr:link href="/voltaireCandide2015/" title="Candide" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/voltaireCandide2015/" display-uri="voltaireCandide2015" type="local">Candide</fr:link></fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>I did very little research prior to reading this book and was not at all aware of what I was getting into. It turns out this book is quite the controversial piece of philosophy. For what was supposed to be a light read, I ended up deep in the weeds on the meaning of life and flaws of humanity. The book is basically a stance against the idea of blind optimisim and the notion that <html:em>everything is as it should be</html:em>. More importantly, even if this were the case (in El Dorado) the human condition would not allow us to simply sit idle in such a place. However, I actually found the conclusion highly inspiring.  <html:em>Cultivate your garden</html:em> - life will not</html:p>
                <html:p>For what it is, I think it is a 7/10.</html:p>
                <html:figure><html:img width="50%" src="/bafkrmica2bnzujxbtqb4phuykwp3j3er55nvara4quzwb5s3hpdbpg4e3q.jpg" />
<html:figcaption /></html:figure>
              </fr:mainmatter>
