                <fr:route>/2I8C/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Review: Elon Musk">Review: <fr:link href="/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" title="Elon Musk" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" display-uri="isaacsonElonMusk2023" type="local">Elon Musk</fr:link></fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>If nothing else, this book made me realize I need to work harder. I am not sure that daddy issues is a sufficient explanation for some of Musk's highly erratic actions. However, it is indisputable the drive and work ethic he both has and demands from his companies. I often wonder whether a relentless tyrant like Musk could maximize my potential, but it is very apparent here that it would come at a severe cost. Getting back to the book, I think it felt a little propaganda-y. I find it hard to believe Elon is a pure intentioned savior of humanity. Though, I do not doubt he likes to seem himself that way.</html:p>
                <html:p>Twitter part was too long, 5/10.</html:p>
