              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter><html:p>This is the first official entry into my <fr:link href="/007S/" title="Weeknotes" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/007S/" display-uri="007S" type="local">Weeknotes</fr:link>! The infrastructure has long been in development, but I have been too lazy / scared to actually start making / publicizing these.</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>20</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/NQFF/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>NQFF</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/NQFF/</fr:route><fr:title text="The Quantified Me: 2026-W29"><fr:link href="/G944/" title="The Quantified Me" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G944/" display-uri="G944" type="local">The Quantified Me</fr:link>: 2026-W29</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>This week I spent the large majority of my time taking notes in this forest. We can see this via the 23hr spent on my forest throughout the week. Admittedly, some of this was spent purely on aesthetic re-design / cleanup, which I hope to not have to do this week. Lab corresponds to my kernel learning, where I spent what appears to be ~5hr implementing a few of the <fr:link href="/tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019/" title="Triton: An intermediate language and compiler for tiled neural network computations" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019/" display-uri="tilletTritonIntermediateLanguage2019" type="local">Triton</fr:link> tutorials, including GEMM. I played around with excalidraw and took some notes <fr:link href="/OGCRV/" title="Memory Tiling (GPU)" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/OGCRV/" display-uri="OGCRV" type="local">here</fr:link>. With this, I began looking into the <fr:link href="/5PSC/" title="Kernel DSLs" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5PSC/" display-uri="5PSC" type="local">Kernel DSLs</fr:link> landscape along with <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link>.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmic3viipl233xukcfg4c63uxyrroaa5caodxqtacfsaoo5c577kpxu.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Coding hours for week 2026-W29.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>
Outside of coding, I did not spend too much time brain-rotting. My phone screentime has also gotten remarkably low, so the issue is not really wasting time doomscrolling / watching youtube, etc. Instead, the problem is just a lack of maintained focus. I bounce between things too frequently, failing to get as much done as I should. I hope to remedy this by being disciplined with pomodoro blocks but early attempts have not been too promising.
</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmicnyfqllwbw6jgi2ne6oagacwzfid2zlqgjmdmvvyq3h5n7mudcl4.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Non-coding computer time for week 2026-W29.</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>20</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/QBM9/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>QBM9</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/QBM9/</fr:route><fr:title text="Life Maxing: 2026-W29"><fr:link href="/5501/" title="Life Maxing" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5501/" display-uri="5501" type="local">Life Maxing</fr:link>: 2026-W29</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>I have been on a remarkable streak of bad luck when trying to run. During vacation (the 3 mile week), there was a heatwave going on throughout Europe. Then, upon my return, I got wildly sick (still managed to get to 30 miles but my Garmin did not like it). Then, this most recent week the Canadian wildfires made Michigan look like a scene out of Chernobyl. I tried to run, but my eyes began watering as soon as I got outside. Hopefully, I can get back on track and scale back up to 40mpw and then to 50+ before we get too close to the marathon.
</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmicjkqerv454jchd6sym7irbhfmllws7qubpj4bcvglrsg4ri4syba.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Health stats for week 2026-W29.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>In other news, I seem to be getting pretty consistent with my habits. I have remarkably caught up on my Anki deck and now need to do more exploratory study to have enough cards each day. The to-do list has not been as life-changing as I hoped as I still struggle to adhere to it on a daily basis. One reason is I think I am too ambitious and should instead start with just one must get done thing each day.</html:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>20</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/K7MF/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>K7MF</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/K7MF/</fr:route><fr:title text="Reading Corner: 2026-W29"><fr:link href="/RPP0/" title="Reading Corner" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RPP0/" display-uri="RPP0" type="local">Reading Corner</fr:link>: 2026-W29</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>I have begun reading <fr:link href="/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" title="Gödel, Escher, Bach: An Eternal Goden Braid" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" display-uri="hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999" type="local">Gödel, Escher, Bach: An Eternal Goden Braid</fr:link> and am really enjoying it. It is strangely refreshing having the math I learned so rigorously distilled into much more digestible chunks. I have also gotten halfway through <fr:link href="/voltaireCandide2015/" title="Candide" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/voltaireCandide2015/" display-uri="voltaireCandide2015" type="local">Candide</fr:link>, which is a very different read (thoughts coming soon).
</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>15</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/HGRL/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>HGRL</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/HGRL/</fr:route><fr:title text="Review: The Mezzanine">Review: <fr:link href="/bakerMezzanine1990/" title="The Mezzanine" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/bakerMezzanine1990/" display-uri="bakerMezzanine1990" type="local">The Mezzanine</fr:link></fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>This was a very different read for me. A short book (only 135 pages) that goes into great detail the work day at the Mezzanine. I have some gripes with the description of <html:em>readable</html:em> on the cover. I found the incredibly vivid imagery sometimes hard to follow. It seems the intent of the book was to highlight the thoughts of an ordinary working man throughout the day. However, some of these thoughs were so far from ordinary it lost the relatable, funny read it was going for. Some chapters were pure gold (the urinal) but others were a huge miss for me.</html:p><html:p>Overall, I enjoyed the book and would recommend. 6.5/10.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="30%" src="/bafkrmib3htjmf6hdfuplcw7m43mtjg34v4oq4pku4jupo4lwgkt2f4njym.jpg" />
<html:figcaption>One of many book covers. Not the best IMO.</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>
  <fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>17</fr:day></fr:date><fr:title text="Goals for Next Week">Goals for Next Week</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter>
<html:p>I completed a <fr:link href="/MA2W/" title="Automatic Brrrrr: History and Challenges" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/MA2W/" display-uri="MA2W" type="local">rough outline</fr:link> of the state of kernel generations as far as I am concerned. I hope to make some serious progress on this next week. Namely, I want to have a pretty complete understanding of the Tiled <fr:link href="/5PSC/" title="Kernel DSLs" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5PSC/" display-uri="5PSC" type="local">DSLs</fr:link> portion and where the distinction between each <fr:link href="/5PSC/" title="Kernel DSLs" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5PSC/" display-uri="5PSC" type="local">DSL</fr:link> is made. I would like to deeply understand the Flash attention Triton kernel from the tutorial. Afterwards, moving to <fr:link href="/wangTileLangComposableTiled2025/" title="TileLang: A Composable Tiled Programming Model for AI Systems" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/wangTileLangComposableTiled2025/" display-uri="wangTileLangComposableTiled2025" type="local">TileLang</fr:link> and seeing how / where they draw the line for more optimization opportunity.</html:p>
<html:p>For Reading Corner, I will likely finish <fr:link href="/voltaireCandide2015/" title="Candide" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/voltaireCandide2015/" display-uri="voltaireCandide2015" type="local">Candide</fr:link> and might also finish <fr:link href="/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" title="Elon Musk" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" display-uri="isaacsonElonMusk2023" type="local">Elon Musk</fr:link>, which I have been working on for awhile now. Stay tuned for their <fr:link href="/YJ05/" title="Book Reviews" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/YJ05/" display-uri="YJ05" type="local">reviews</fr:link>!</html:p>
