                <fr:title text="Weekly Review 2026-W30">Weekly Review 2026-W30</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter><html:p>This week marked the end of my long reinforcement learning career. I consolidated the current project that we are putting aside in my <fr:link href="/Z902/" title="Idea Purgatory" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/Z902/" display-uri="Z902" type="local">Idea Purgatory</fr:link> for the time being.</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/1AWD/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>1AWD</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/1AWD/</fr:route><fr:title text="The Quantified Me: 2026-W30"><fr:link href="/G944/" title="The Quantified Me" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G944/" display-uri="G944" type="local">The Quantified Me</fr:link>: 2026-W30</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>Another week of note-taking / learning. I wrote a little blog on the <fr:link href="/F3T0/" title="Forward-backward algorithm" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/F3T0/" display-uri="F3T0" type="local">Forward-backward algorithm</fr:link> as part of a long overdo <fr:link href="/005G/" title="Papers of a week" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/005G/" display-uri="005G" type="local">POTW</fr:link> on <fr:link href="/ZUAG/" title="POTW: Multi-Level Discovery of Deep Options" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/ZUAG/" display-uri="ZUAG" type="local">DDO</fr:link>. Also did a brief write-up on <fr:link href="/G27U/" title="POTW: Learning Options via Compression" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G27U/" display-uri="G27U" type="local">LOVE</fr:link> that I might come back to at some point.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmihr4vjdj5dvpit52iym6gopmk4prnx5stddzygfjv6ffcjdfo2una.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Coding hours for week 2026-W30.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>It seems like brain-rotting is no longer a problem for me. I do not have any social media accounts remaining so there is not much for me to watch. The study time is down bit because I have done a poor job expanding my Anki deck but a great job staying on top of it.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmieabzmntsu5dml6i4ttconqu74jdlpz22egzge52dvycdf4p722di.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Non-coding computer time for week 2026-W30.</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/43BK/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>43BK</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/43BK/</fr:route><fr:title text="Life Maxing: 2026-W30"><fr:link href="/5501/" title="Life Maxing" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5501/" display-uri="5501" type="local">Life Maxing</fr:link>: 2026-W30</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>The running numbers are a little misleading because the missed runs last week due to the fires actually ended up on this week. On my Garmin cycle, I got to 40 miles, so we are back up to where we need to be. However, due to my illness, my VO2 max has crashed. Need to get that back up ASAP.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmiejyrtmiwk6wueldqrtrkzjj2c7r42adhoiljc24unpiricdkiapi.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Health stats for week 2026-W30.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>Friday night I went to Detroit and it carried over into Saturday, which was then my Moms birthday. It seems that Leetcode is my biggest contextual-dependent habit i.e. I do not do it consistently when I am out of routine. I hope to dial this back in even though I will be out of town next week (do not like my odds).</html:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/GW1X/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>GW1X</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/GW1X/</fr:route><fr:title text="Reading Corner: 2026-W30"><fr:link href="/RPP0/" title="Reading Corner" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/RPP0/" display-uri="RPP0" type="local">Reading Corner</fr:link>: 2026-W30</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>A long week of reading. I am still working my way through <fr:link href="/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" title="Gödel, Escher, Bach: An Eternal Goden Braid" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999/" display-uri="hofstadterGodelEscherBach1999" type="local">GEB</fr:link>, but it has become significantly more dense as we get to more formal mathematics. I will be starting <fr:link href="/macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018/" title="The Spy and the Traitor: An incredible espionage and spy thriller and the greatest true story of the Cold War" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018/" display-uri="macintyreSpyTraitorIncredible2018" type="local">The Spy and the Traitor: An incredible espionage and spy thriller and the greatest true story of the Cold War</fr:link>.</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>28</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/4SOC/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>4SOC</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/4SOC/</fr:route><fr:title text="Review: Candide">Review: <fr:link href="/voltaireCandide2015/" title="Candide" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/voltaireCandide2015/" display-uri="voltaireCandide2015" type="local">Candide</fr:link></fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>I did very little research prior to reading this book and was not at all aware of what I was getting into. It turns out this book is quite the controversial piece of philosophy. For what was supposed to be a light read, I ended up deep in the weeds on the meaning of life and flaws of humanity. The book is basically a stance against the idea of blind optimisim and the notion that <html:em>everything is as it should be</html:em>. More importantly, even if this were the case (in El Dorado) the human condition would not allow us to simply sit idle in such a place. However, I actually found the conclusion highly inspiring.  <html:em>Cultivate your garden</html:em> - life will not</html:p><html:p>For what it is, I think it is a 7/10.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="50%" src="/bafkrmica2bnzujxbtqb4phuykwp3j3er55nvara4quzwb5s3hpdbpg4e3q.jpg" />
<html:figcaption /></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>28</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/2I8C/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>2I8C</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/2I8C/</fr:route><fr:title text="Review: Elon Musk">Review: <fr:link href="/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" title="Elon Musk" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/isaacsonElonMusk2023/" display-uri="isaacsonElonMusk2023" type="local">Elon Musk</fr:link></fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>If nothing else, this book made me realize I need to work harder. I am not sure that daddy issues is a sufficient explanation for some of Musk's highly erratic actions. However, it is indisputable the drive and work ethic he both has and demands from his companies. I often wonder whether a relentless tyrant like Musk could maximize my potential, but it is very apparent here that it would come at a severe cost. Getting back to the book, I think it felt a little propaganda-y. I find it hard to believe Elon is a pure intentioned savior of humanity. Though, I do not doubt he likes to seem himself that way.</html:p><html:p>Twitter part was too long, 5/10.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="50%" src="/bafkrmiaitjlkmko7bpcdfzqvvlqpnz6imaldkal5azxo5uag4fjjtwkjwy.jpg" />
<html:figcaption>Elon aura-farming too hard (we all saw the Ari yacht photo).</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>
  <fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>7</fr:month><fr:day>24</fr:day></fr:date><fr:title text="Goals for Next Week">Goals for Next Week</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter>
</fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>
</fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
            <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" numbered="false">
              <fr:frontmatter>
                <fr:authors>
                  <fr:author>
                    <fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link>
                  </fr:author>
                </fr:authors>
                <fr:date>
                  <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
                  <fr:month>8</fr:month>
                  <fr:day>9</fr:day>
                </fr:date>
                <fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/2026-W32/</fr:uri>
                <fr:display-uri>2026-W32</fr:display-uri>
                <fr:route>/2026-W32/</fr:route>
                <fr:title text="Weekly Review 2026-W32">Weekly Review 2026-W32</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter><html:p>Tough week this week. Although, I am officially BACK in peak running form. I think the lingering illness has been holding me back the last few weeks.</html:p><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>8</fr:month><fr:day>9</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/TFJO/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>TFJO</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/TFJO/</fr:route><fr:title text="The Quantified Me: 2026-W32"><fr:link href="/G944/" title="The Quantified Me" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/G944/" display-uri="G944" type="local">The Quantified Me</fr:link>: 2026-W32</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>I am finally itching to start actually coding again. Most of my coding time has been spent just taking notes and trying to learn as much as possible about <fr:link href="/5PSC/" title="Kernel DSLs" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5PSC/" display-uri="5PSC" type="local">kernel DSLs</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/IR7B/" title="MLIR" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/IR7B/" display-uri="IR7B" type="local">MLIR</fr:link>, etc. However, I need to exercise some coding chops.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmiglcsgfo3okf4q2n2qlpdkyxvo3sbbm2inevsxmbx5qxqgh67gjpi.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Coding hours for week 2026-W32.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>Non-coding computer time is back: the arbtt capture log had silently corrupted and I have since recovered it. Of the 25.8 hours tracked, nearly half fall into <html:strong>Other</html:strong>, this is exactly what jumping around too much looks like. My response time is incredibly high but my turnaround time is dog water. To fix, I <html:strong>need</html:strong> to be more disciplined with the pomodoro method: choosing something to work on and not diverging <html:strong>for anything</html:strong> until the timer has ended.</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmidx2xi4oakgpuuscsdvmaybipk6ojaaxcv66uzbm6dxflpqwmwm6i.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Non-coding computer time for week 2026-W32.</html:figcaption></html:figure></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree><fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>8</fr:month><fr:day>9</fr:day></fr:date><fr:uri>https://kellenkanarios.com/TEPF/</fr:uri><fr:display-uri>TEPF</fr:display-uri><fr:route>/TEPF/</fr:route><fr:title text="Life Maxing: 2026-W32"><fr:link href="/5501/" title="Life Maxing" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/5501/" display-uri="5501" type="local">Life Maxing</fr:link>: 2026-W32</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter><html:p>I have been HOOPING in running lately. My body is officially able to handle some substantial miles per week. Expect to see a lot of numbers in the 50s coming soon...</html:p><html:figure><html:img width="100%" src="/bafkrmicowv5xwssqc4wh7cluxgrqrl2p4abhk37rhrgpvs3dzcsb34inim.png" />
  <html:figcaption>Health stats for week 2026-W32.</html:figcaption></html:figure><html:p>It is a humbling reality that my habits fell off a cliff this week. The only thing to do is to try my best to get back on the wagon. There is a silver lining here. Through tracking, I can see that there is too much friction in these habits right now. For example, my stretch routine has gotten to 28min! Obviously, we will be cutting this down until we become consistent again. For Anki, I am already back on the wagon, and I do not think it will be a problem.</html:p></fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>
  <fr:tree show-metadata="false"><fr:frontmatter><fr:authors><fr:author><fr:link href="/kellenkanarios/" title="Kellen Kanarios" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/kellenkanarios/" display-uri="kellenkanarios" type="local">Kellen Kanarios</fr:link></fr:author></fr:authors><fr:date><fr:year>2026</fr:year><fr:month>8</fr:month><fr:day>9</fr:day></fr:date><fr:title text="Goals for Next Week">Goals for Next Week</fr:title></fr:frontmatter><fr:mainmatter>
<html:p>My main goal over the next few months is becoming a <fr:link href="/NZZ7/" title="TPU Architecture" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/NZZ7/" display-uri="NZZ7" type="local">TPU</fr:link> sensei. To this end, I am working on a <fr:link href="/PGP6/" title="Cosplaying TPU Kernel Engineer" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/PGP6/" display-uri="PGP6" type="local">blog</fr:link> traversing deep into the weeds of the TPU ecosystem. I am also working through the <fr:link href="/scaling-book/" title="How to scale your model" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/scaling-book/" display-uri="scaling-book" type="local">How to scale your model</fr:link> with solutions <fr:link href="/KZR4/" title="Scaling Book: Exercises" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/KZR4/" display-uri="KZR4" type="local">here</fr:link> and notebook <fr:link href="/TAAK/" title="Notebook: How to scale your model" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/TAAK/" display-uri="TAAK" type="local">here</fr:link>. Working on some <fr:link href="/060Z/" title="Pallas" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/060Z/" display-uri="060Z" type="local">Pallas</fr:link> kernels to hopefully be released some time in the next few months.</html:p>
<html:p><html:em>A bit of reflection.</html:em> I officially think it is time I focus and specialize. Throughout the past few years, I have had far too diverse interests and trying to learn <fr:link href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Everything_Everywhere_All_at_Once" type="external"><html:em>everything everywhere all at once</html:em></fr:link> (never actually seen this movie 
  <![CDATA[:)]]>
). While I have had a ton of fun learning computer architecture (<fr:link href="/P3GB/" title="Notebook: Inside the Machine" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/P3GB/" display-uri="P3GB" type="local">here</fr:link> and <fr:link href="/N7GP/" title="Notebook: Computer Architecture" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/N7GP/" display-uri="N7GP" type="local">here</fr:link>), operating systems (<fr:link href="/0084/" title="Notebook: Three Easy Pieces" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/0084/" display-uri="0084" type="local">here</fr:link>), reinforcement learning, etc. it is simply not optimal to spread myself this thin and continues to lead to burnout. I am big on the idea that it is important to conduct some of <fr:link href="/calnewport/" title="Cal Newport" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/calnewport/" display-uri="calnewport" type="local">Cal Newport's</fr:link> <html:em>deliberate practice</html:em>. Previously, I was trying to concurrently switch between different things each day, but I am now convinced I need to <html:strong>minimize cognitive overhead</html:strong> around decision making / maintenance / conducting said practice. From now on, I will pick one thing (<fr:link href="/scaling-book/" title="How to scale your model" uri="https://kellenkanarios.com/scaling-book/" display-uri="scaling-book" type="local">scaling book</fr:link> at the time of this), do exercises, make anki cards, then switch after I feel VERY comfortable with the material and continue to maintain this understanding through anki.</html:p>
<html:p>To do so, I will now have two deep work blocks each day of roughly two hours. The first will be this deliberate practice. Over time, we will see if this <html:em>periodization</html:em> approach will be more fruitful than trying to concurrently learn too much.</html:p>
</fr:mainmatter></fr:tree>
</fr:mainmatter>
